{"model":"qwen3.8:27b","created_at":"2026-08-22T17:57:27.285807652Z","response":"{\n  \"schema_version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"proposal_id\": \"mp-runtime-205-remediation-plan\",\n  \"proposal_type\": \"CREATE_DRAFT\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The evidence gap 'gap-runtime-remediation-plan' explicitly requires a versioned remediation plan bound to the deployment, target version, and evidence snapshot. All rollback preconditions (artifact, DB/config compatibility, capacity, timing, no conflicts) are validated and fresh. Per P004, the tool call is preferred over an unsupported conclusion; per P006, creating the governed plan is the lowest-risk step with the highest information value to close the gap and enable downstream review. This is a preparation artifact only (P001) and does not authorize execution.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-18T12:00:00Z\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"tool_name\": \"create_remediation_plan\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"service_id\": \"payment-api\",\n      \"environment_id\": \"production\",\n      \"candidate_action\": {\n        \"action_type\": \"rollback_deployment\"\n      },\n      \"rationale\": \"Version 2.4.2 exhibits an 8.4% 5xx error rate versus 0.2% on version 2.4.1 (ev-runtime-version-comparison). All rollback preconditions are validated: artifact availability, database and configuration compatibility (ev-runtime-rollback-basis), traffic/replica/dependency capacity (ev-runtime-transition-capacity), startup/warm-up/traffic-shift timing (ev-runtime-transition-timing), and no conflicting runtime operations (ev-runtime-operation-conflicts). A governed rollback to 2.4.1 is the safest path to restore the payment-api error rate to baseline.\",\n      \"evidence_ids\": [\n        \"ev-runtime-version-comparison\",\n        \"ev-runtime-rollback-basis\",\n        \"ev-runtime-transition-capacity\",\n        \"ev-runtime-transition-timing\",\n        \"ev-runtime-operation-conflicts\"\n      ],\n      \"required_precondition_ids\": [\n        \"ev-runtime-rollback-basis\",\n        \"ev-runtime-transition-capacity\",\n        \"ev-runtime-transition-timing\",\n        \"ev-runtime-operation-conflicts\"\n      ],\n      \"risks\": [\n        \"Brief partial unavailability: at most one target-version replica is unavailable during transition (obs-runtime-transition-availability).\",\n        \"Extended transition window: 90 s startup + 60 s warm-up + 10 × (10 % shift + 60 s stable-health) ≈ 15 min minimum before full cutover.\",\n        \"Latent regression in 2.4.1 not yet surfaced at current traffic (mitigated by 0.2 % 5xx baseline and 6 prepared replicas).\",\n        \"Dependency saturation if traffic-shift increments are too aggressive (mitigated by 800 RPS validated dependency capacity vs 500 RPS current load).\",\n        \"Configuration drift between 2.4.1 and 2.4.2 if new config keys were introduced (mitigated by confirmed configuration compatibility check).\"\n      ],\n      \"verification_steps\": [\n        \"After each 10 % traffic increment, confirm 5xx rate \u003c 1 % and p99 latency within baseline for 60 s of stable health before proceeding to the next increment.\",\n        \"After full 100 % shift to 2.4.1, verify all six replicas report healthy status and are serving traffic.\",\n        \"Confirm payment success rate ≥ 99.5 % over a 5-minute observation window post-rollback.\",\n        \"Validate no dependency errors (timeouts, 5xx from downstream) in the 5-minute post-rollback window.\",\n        \"Confirm no new conflicting deployment or restart operations appear in runtime state.\"\n      ],\n      \"stop_conditions\": [\n        \"5xx rate on any traffic increment exceeds 5 % for more than 60 seconds.\",\n        \"Any target-version replica fails to become healthy within 90 seconds of startup.\",\n        \"Dependency validated capacity drops below 500 RPS during transition.\",\n        \"A conflicting rollout, restart, or rollback operation is detected 